Description: pct move-volume --with-snapshots for Proxmox VE
 Proxmox refuses "pct move-volume" whenever a volume has snapshots, vzdump
 restore drops snapshot history, and the only snapshot-preserving paths are
 same-storage-type node migrations. There is no cross-storage-type story.
 .
 This adds a --with-snapshots option that moves a container volume to another
 storage while preserving its snapshots, by replaying them oldest-to-newest
 through Proxmox's own copy machinery. Storage-agnostic: any source whose
 snapshots PVE can mount, any target that supports snapshots.
 .
 It also stops rsync copying filesystem-internal virtual xattrs, which
 otherwise abort a copy off a bcachefs-backed storage onto any other
 filesystem with EOPNOTSUPP.
 .
 Patches are applied all-or-nothing and re-applied after pve-container
 upgrades. Intended as an upstream RFC, not a permanent out-of-tree patch.
